W30 = 《网络交易监督管理办法》 (SAMR order No.37, promulgated 2021-03-15, effective 2021-05-01, AMENDED by SAMR order No.101 dated 2025-03-18), official fulltext direct-captured A-grade from samr.gov.cn (zw/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/fgs/art/2025/art_4b47c79b8d994a42bba4835997688faa.html, page published 2025-04-03; search located it in 1 try, 1 direct get, zero extra negatives). The amendment matters: capturing the amended current text avoids citing the superseded 2021 wording.
Key clauses entered: art.2 scope includes online social/live commerce; art.7 platform-operator definition covers social/live services providing venue, product browsing, order generation, online payment; art.8 individual annual turnover <= CNY 100k registration exemption; art.13 no blanket/default/bundled consent and itemized consent for sensitive data; art.14 four false-promotion bans (fabricated transactions/reviews, review-order manipulation, fake stock/booking/rush marketing, fabricated traffic and like/tip data); art.15 technical handling of prohibited content inside reviews (not deletion); art.16 commercial messages require prior consent/request, true identity and contact, conspicuous simple free opt-out, immediate stop on refusal and no re-sending under another name; art.17 bundling must be conspicuous and never defaulted, past choices cannot seed later defaults; art.18 auto-renewal requires conspicuous notice BOTH before acceptance and before each renewal date, consumer choice, plus a conspicuous simple cancel/change option at any time during service and no unreasonable fees; art.19 full/true/accurate/timely disclosure; art.20 social/live sellers must display product, actual operator and after-sales info, and live video must be kept >= 3 years from stream end; art.21 six format-clause bans (repair/return/refund/compensation exclusions, barring complaints/litigation, barring contract change/termination, one-sided final interpretation, etc.); art.23 self-termination requires 30-day prior conspicuous notice; art.24 onboarding identity/address/contact/licence verification with re-verification at least every 6 months; arts.25/26 semi-annual reporting (January and July) plus 3-day change filing and 7-day platform re-verification; art.28 three years of historical platform-rule versions must be kept and be readable/downloadable before a rule change takes effect; art.31 identity records >= 3 years after exit and transaction records >= 3 years from completion; art.41 penalties (CNY 30k ceiling for arts.13/16/18-cl.2; arts.18-cl.1/21 handled under Consumer Protection Regulation art.50).
